                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="482-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Ningbo Alctron Electronics Co., Ltd. HSMC001</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Cardioid Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>An inexpensive side-address condenser, this mic has a cardioid pickup pattern and an internally-switched high pass filter.</p><p>Like all Alctron products, it is not typically available direct from the manufacturer, but rather through a number of European and North American &#8220;rebadgers.&#8221; For example, the HSMC001W is visually identical to, and believed to be the source of the Apex Electronics model 435 condenser.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Alctron/HSMC001W">Ningbo Alctron Electronics Co., Ltd. HSMC001</a> is also known as: HSMC001WA, HSMC001, MC001.</p>
